-- Fixture for the `l4 export --to=dmn --fail-on` threshold tests: a DMN
-- report that is blocking-ONLY (2 blocking, 0 lossy, 0 advisory).
--
-- Two decisions whose bodies are BOOLEAN ORDERINGS: FEEL's comparison
-- operators are defined over numbers/strings/dates and NOT booleans (DMN 1.3
-- Table 54), so `p AT LEAST q` has no FEEL rendering, goes out verbatim, and
-- D-LITERALEXPR reports at Blocking -- and nothing else fires (no MAYBE, no
-- rename, no fixture, no regulative body).
--
-- (History of this role: export-two-rules.l4's regulative decides played it
-- until Phase 4's population filter routed uncalled regulative bodies out of
-- the DRG; then two arithmetic formulas played it, until the Phase 5 severity
-- re-key correctly made an EXECUTABLE boxed literal Advisory rather than
-- Blocking -- D-LITERALEXPR is Blocking only where the emitted text is raw L4
-- no engine can evaluate, which a boolean ordering is.)

ASSUME p IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME q IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p dominates` MEANS p AT LEAST q

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`q dominates` MEANS q AT LEAST p
